{
  "requirement": "The Habeas Codicem book MUST configure mdBook's Git repository link for `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem` and its page edit links for the `main` branch.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. `book.toml` MUST set mdBook's Git repository link to `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem`. It MUST also set page edit links for the `main` branch.\n\n`tests/repository.rs#fn[book_links_to_the_repository_and_main_branch_edit_pages]` is marked `{test}` for the requirement. It parses `book.toml` through the `repository_toml` helper, which reads the file and parses it as TOML. It then makes two exact-equality assertions on `output.habeas.html`:\n- `git-repository-url` equals `https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem`. This covers the repository link.\n- `edit-url-template` equals `https://github.com/nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem/edit/main/{path}`. This covers the edit links, including the `main` branch and the right repository.\n\nA wrong repository, a wrong branch, or a missing key would fail one of these assertions. A quick search of `book.toml` shows both keys under `[output.habeas.html]`. That is the same table the test reads, and the `{impl}` markers sit on those two pairs.\n\nThe requirement is a static configuration value, so there are no other input classes, boundaries or failure modes to test. I found no gaps.",
  "references": "18c39a5f2ef5c6c6fff59ced94783e52c7eded7ec1513a5943cb026ff89a8950",
